{"availability":"available","full":"rajak312/splitease","name":"splitease","description":"Split shared expenses — one React Native (Expo) codebase for iOS, Android & web, GraphQL Yoga + Pothos + Prisma API","category":"Finance","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T07:14:30Z","updated":"2026-10-08T07:14:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://splitease-lalit.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:32.955Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:32.955Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:32.955Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:35:32.955Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SplitEase is a Splitwise-style app for shared costs: trips, flats, office lunches. One React Native codebase runs on iOS, Android and the web, backed by a code-first GraphQL API. It covers four split modes (equal, exact, percentage, shares), debt simplification, multi-currency groups, realtime updates and an offline-friendly cache.","Live demo — click “Try the demo”. You get a private sandbox with sample groups, no sign-up needed.","More in docs/screenshots/ (dark mode, welcome page, expense list)."],"features":["One codebase, three platforms. Expo SDK 57, Expo Router and Tamagui. On wide screens (desktop web, tablets) the app shows a sidebar; on phones it uses bottom tabs. Haptics on native, dark mode everywhere.","GraphQL done properly. GraphQL Yoga with Pothos (code-first, Prisma plugin, Relay connections, scope auth). Typed client documents come from GraphQL Code Generator, and urql uses Graphcache for a normalised cache.","Money is never a float. Every amount is an integer in minor units (paise, cents). Rounding remainders are assigned with the largest-remainder method, so splits always add up to the exact total. The same split code runs…","Debt simplification. A greedy net-balance algorithm turns a web of IOUs into at most n − 1 payments, e.g. “Rahul pays you ₹6,456.83”. Property-based tests check that money is conserved.","Production-minded auth. Argon2id password hashing and 15-minute JWT access tokens. Refresh tokens are opaque, stored only as an HMAC, rotated on every use, and reuse of an old token revokes the whole token family.…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rajak312/splitease/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"75546f910ed3c977d68994ba4ff71ff94c62f33b7e6cc9aa8c3b05fa44f17784","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:33.021Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:33.021Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SplitEase is a Splitwise-style app for shared costs: trips, flats, office lunches. One React Native codebase runs on iOS, Android and the web, backed by a code-first GraphQL API. It covers four split modes (equal, exact, percentage, shares), debt simplification, multi-currency groups, realtime updates and an offline-friendly cache.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rajak312/splitease/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Auth: email + password sign-up and login, plus one-tap “Try the demo”.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rajak312/splitease/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"API: sign-up/login, argon2id hashing, refresh rotation, reuse detection revoking the family, a concurrent-refresh race, expiry, logout; group create/join/invite reset; all split modes end-to-end; validation errors; balances checked against the pure function; settle-up bringing balances to zero; edit/delete with activity log; pagination, search and category filters; dashboard…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rajak312/splitease/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"API: sign-up/login, argon2id hashing, refresh rotation, reuse detection revoking the family, a concurrent-refresh race, expiry, logout; group create/join/invite reset; all split modes end-to-end; validation err